// Wall-normal profile lines on the SUCTION surface at the Phase-1 stations
// x/c = 0.05 0.07 0.10 0.15 0.20 0.30 0.40 0.50 0.60 0.70 0.80 0.90.
// TWO lines per station, both starting a hair off the wall (so the first
// sample lands inside the first cell, not on the boundary face), along the
// LOCAL surface normal:
//   bl_x###_inner -- dense sublayer line, ~2x the d99 estimate long at
//                    ~1e-5 m pitch. The outer line alone puts ~2.5e-4 m
//                    between samples while the y+ = 1 first cell is ~8e-6 m,
//                    so the entire resolved sublayer would fall between its
//                    first two points.
//   bl_x###       -- outer line, 0.15 c / 600 points, comfortably past
//                    delta even at high AoA; captures the BL edge and the
//                    outer flow the edge-detection guard needs.
// The builder computes anchors and normals from the same resampled
// LS(1)-0413 loop the mesh was built from, so the lines track the actual
// surface. Downstream, scripts/extract_bl.py MERGES each inner/outer pair
// (sorted by wall distance, deduplicated) and integrates the result into
// the delta / delta* table that sizes the VGs (spec Phase-1 item 5).

blProfiles
{
    type            sets;
    libs            (sampling);

    // Sample once, from the CONVERGED solution: profiles from a half-
    // converged state would poison the VG-sizing table.
    writeControl    onEnd;

    interpolationScheme cellPoint;

    // raw = plain numeric columns; trivially parsed by the Phase-1
    // BL-extraction script with numpy.loadtxt.
    setFormat       raw;

    fields          (U p k omega nut gammaInt ReThetat);

    sets
    (
@SAMPLING_SETS@
    );
}

